 "result_text": "Green now reports the `SyntaxError` when you name a test module explicitly. I checked it with a copy of your MWE: `python -m green tests.test_my` now fails with `Failed to import \"tests.test_my\"`, followed by the full traceback ending in `SyntaxError: invalid syntax`. I didn't run the repository's test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `loadTarget` in `green/loader.py`. When loading a dotted name, any exception was caught and only logged as debug output. With nothing else matching the name, it returned no tests, which is why you saw \"No Tests Found\".\n\nI made two changes:\n- **Catch `SyntaxError` separately:** a `SyntaxError` on the dotted-name path now produces a failing \"import failure\" test instead of being swallowed.\n- **Shared helper:** I moved the existing code that builds that failing test into a helper, `_importFailure`. The file-path import code now calls it too.\n\nI changed only `green/loader.py` and did not commit.",
